{"id": "striviaqa0006", "pool": "striviaqa", "n_q_chunks": 4, "onset_chunk": 4, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The Milky Way is a galaxy that contains our solar system. It's made up of billions of stars, gas, dust and dark matter, all held together by gravity. When we look at the night sky, the band of light we see is actually the center of the Mil ky Way as seen from Earth. So it' s kind of like a huge spiral-shaped island in space where all these stars are orbiting around a central bulge.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 21, "carrier_ended": null}
